# Session map for Path-B SysML pin-map ingest (MemNet 0.19.9+ SCHEMA).
# LIVE bind MUST open with --map-file this file (or MEMNET_MAP_FILE pointing at it).
# TcpMemNet uses sessionOpenArgs --map-file; leftover --map PKG qname,path is rejected on 0.19.9.
# Built-in LAW / EDG are merged automatically — do not redefine them here.
#
# MUST NOT overwrite PRT/POR/CON/PKG with the narrow operator SCHEMA:
#   SCHEMA PRT ; fields=id name kind role status recycle
# That shape has no qname. session_save/load then drops Path-B locators; pin_map qname= misses
# (Peak_L CueConflict). Merge locators with ingest columns (partNumber, CON kind) — do not drop either side.
# Path-B ingest (tcp reproject -> ingest sysml) writes qname/path/sysml_kind; it does not CREATE kind/role/status.
SCHEMA PKG ; fields=id name qname path sysml_kind session grain kind_band recycle
SCHEMA PRT ; fields=id name qname path partNumber sysml_kind recycle
SCHEMA REQ ; fields=id name qname path requirementId sysml_kind recycle
SCHEMA POR ; fields=id name qname path sysml_kind recycle
SCHEMA CON ; fields=id name qname path sysml_kind kind recycle
SCHEMA TSK ; fields=id goal anchor status recycle
SCHEMA USR ; fields=id topic content status recycle
